Approach: Use sliding window with frequency array to track counts of 'a', 'b', and 'c'. When all three are present, count all valid substrings from current right and shrink the window.

Time Complexity: O(n) — each character is added and removed at most once.

Space Complexity: O(1) — fixed-size frequency array used.

class Solution {
    public int numberOfSubstrings(String s) {
        int left=0,right=0,count=0,n=s.length();
        int freq[]=new int[3];
        while(right<n){
           freq[s.charAt(right)-'a']++;
           while(freq[0]>0 && freq[1]>0 && freq[2]>0){
            count+=n-right;
            freq[s.charAt(left)-'a']--;
            left++;
           }
           right++;
        }
        return count;
